### **What happens when you hit COMPILE SCENE:**

1.  **The "Cleaning" happens:** The text box will display the cleaned-up version of your story/code, stripping away the symbols.
2.  **The "Pulse" activates:** On the right side, under **LIVE PULSE FEED**, you will see five distinct events appear in real-time, mapping each symbol to its machine action (e.g., `⚡` becomes `INCREASE_PACE`, `◈` becomes `LOCK_CANON`, etc.).
3.  **The Console logs:** If you press `F12` (or right-click -> Inspect -> Console), you will see the system physically running those events one by one.

If you see those events pop up on the right, the Engine is fully bonded to your UI. **Does the Pulse feed show up as expected when you compile?**
